416	FACTS.md:162
417	- **The specification gives the run-time instance of a dispatched declaration by the POPL 2019 paper's rule, a lone type parameter with no narrowest candidate its bound, and reads a `comprises` clause at the level of values in every passage** (`compile-ladder/rung-spec-overloading/decision-record.md`; POSITIONS, "A type parameter the arguments do not fix takes its bound, never `Bottom` (the paper's instance rule)." and "The `comprises` passages read at the level of values (PLAN item 26, row 491)"). The dispatch paragraph (`Specification/basic/overloading.tex:312-332`): the declaration the static call selected runs at its inferred instance, any other at the intersection of its upper bounds, fixed by the value at an invariant position, never `BottomType` nor the union; its callout (`:333-349`) says both implementations take the value's type (row 538, `compiler_tests/XXXGenericInstanceUnfixed`). The inference chapter gives a lone type parameter with no narrowest candidate its bound (`basic/inference.tex:89-98`), its Appendix I entry listing the checker's departures (rows 508, 515, 516, 518, 541). Under item 26 covering is defined (`basic/types-vals-vars.tex:590-601`), the Meet Rule has its closed-trait case for functions and functional methods, a call between two closed traits is typed by the meet of its candidates' return types where none has static parameters (rows 540, 543, 546, 547), and the proof appendix marks row 487's closure assumption (`Specification/appendices/overloading-function.tex`).
